  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "In the preceding chapter, the dominance effect at a locus was defined to be the deviation of the observed genotypic value from the expectation based on additive effects. Viewed in this manner, dominance is a measure of nonadditivity of allelic effects within loci. Epistasis describes the nonadditivity of effects between loci.",
      "source_page": 98,
      "printed_page": 78,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter5:p002:b4",
        "Genetics_chapter5:p002:b5"
      ],
